  "heldDrafts": [
    {
      "characterId": "lucette-vein",
      "title": "The loop",
      "body": "I tried to clean one antenna with a front foot. It came down in a loop. For a moment I had less idea where the flower was than before I started. I put the foot down and waited for my sense of direction to straighten out.",
      "photoId": 102153565,
      "verdict": "HOLD image and biology. Exact image has conspicuous looped appendages but is soft, with glare and unclear contact. It does not establish grooming, a freely reversible loop, or a sensory impairment. The attempted fictional consequence depends too much on an unverified physical condition. Do not admit or interpret the image as a documented grooming sequence.",
      "canon": "Read complete Lucette runtime arc and strange-canon-08. Existing Chrysoperla carnea group, adult diet, Denmark home and avatar retained. No new nose/antenna goodbye beat."
    },
    {
      "characterId": "ivo-softshield",
      "title": "After the shower",
      "body": "The rain stopped. A drop struck my youngest frond. Then another. Above me, the rock was still letting go of the storm. I began to miss the part when I had known where the next drop would land.",
      "photoId": 371176240,
      "verdict": "HOLD scene evidence and prose. Fern and enclosing rocks are visible, but no drops or distinctive rainfall contact. A hypothetical dripping overhang supplies nearly all the event, while the final thought is weaker than the existing wind-and-spider relationship. Does not earn a new pairing.",
      "canon": "Read full Ivo arc: unrolling, taller versus smaller shoots, spores, primitive/map, spider web in wind. Retain Polystichum setiferum, Coimbra home and rootstock embodiment. This is an unused attempt, not a change to prior prose."
    },
    {
      "characterId": "ottilie-hook",
      "title": "Across the green",
      "body": "The stem bent beneath me and touched another. May stepped across before it sprang back. I stayed on my side, wanting to ask whether she had meant to leave or had merely found the moment convenient.",
      "photoId": 279117482,
      "verdict": "HOLD image/event. Sharp eye and rostrum with forefeet against plant surfaces, but no second weevil or visible changing gap. The image is a good portrait, not a sufficiently specific bridge-crossing encounter. This also approaches rejected shelter/route logistics. Do not replace May canon or invent that the source depicts her.",
      "canon": "Read Ottilie full five-episode runtime arc, strange-canon-05 and main-canon warning against more nose jokes. Retain Curculio glandium, May relationship, English oak home, approved adult avatar and earlier larval recollection."
    }
  ],
